# Virtual Environment
# The glob matters: a second interpreter's environment sitting beside .venv used to be copied
# into the image by `COPY . .`, so the build context — and the layer hash — depended on which
# throwaway virtualenvs the author happened to have on disk.
.env
.venv
.venv*
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Docker
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Testing and tool caches
# Every entry below is a local artifact the runtime never reads. They were listed in .gitignore
# but not here, so they stayed out of git and went into the image anyway.
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tiktoken_cache/

# Development surface with no reader in any Docker stage
# 2026-08-24: verified none of these are imported by project/ or alembic/, and no COPY in the
# Dockerfile (any stage, including functional-tests) names them — the exact command is on the
# `runtime-base` copy list in the Dockerfile, next to the files that DO need to survive
# (.env.sample, pyproject.toml). Excluding a path here removes it from the build CONTEXT, so it is
# gone for every stage at once, not just `app` — that is why tests/ is deliberately NOT listed
# below even though it is equally a development artifact. tests/ has a reader: the
# functional-tests stage. It is kept out of the image the same way the rest of this section is —
# by never landing in `app` — but through a selective COPY in the Dockerfile instead of an
# .dockerignore line, because functional-tests still needs it from the builder. See the Dockerfile
# comment on that COPY before adding tests/ here.
#
# scripts/ and ai_context/ are missing from the list below for the same reason as tests/ and by the
# same route: the functional suite imports them, so they have to reach the build context, and they
# are kept out of `app` by the selective COPY instead. Which test imports what, and what breaks the
# day someone adds them here, is written once beside that COPY in the Dockerfile. ai_query/ has no
# reader in tests/ and so does stay listed.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.github/
.githooks/
ai_query/
docs/
README.md
PROJECT.md
CODEOWNERS
LICENSE
Makefile
pytest.ini
dev_setup.sh
docker-compose.postgres.yml
